1
00:01:42,770 --> 00:01:44,610
Kamen Lion

2
00:01:44,820 --> 00:01:48,110
No, we're going to watch Cats of Japan!

3
00:01:49,990 --> 00:01:52,030
Stop that!

4
00:01:53,030 --> 00:01:54,740
Are you fighting over the TV again?

5
00:01:54,740 --> 00:01:56,330
Doraemon started it...

6
00:01:56,950 --> 00:01:58,950
It's Nobita's fault...

7
00:02:01,330 --> 00:02:02,290
STOP IT!

8
00:02:03,870 --> 00:02:05,130
Honestly...

9
00:02:05,210 --> 00:02:07,790
I'm going to cut that TV in half one of these days.

10
00:02:10,260 --> 00:02:13,130
That's a good idea!

11
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:16,680
Dividing Blade

12
00:02:21,510 --> 00:02:23,850
No, don't!

13
00:02:24,730 --> 00:02:25,770
Ahh!

14
00:02:26,270 --> 00:02:26,730
Hmm?

15
00:02:27,690 --> 00:02:28,690
There's two of them!

16
00:02:28,810 --> 00:02:33,440
Haha! This tool splits anything it cuts into two!

17
00:02:33,610 --> 00:02:34,530
Wow!

18
00:02:38,190 --> 00:02:40,410
Whoa! It really works!

19
00:02:41,240 --> 00:02:42,620
It's a bit small, but...

20
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:50,000
Nobita, Shizuka chan is on the phone.

21
00:02:50,250 --> 00:02:50,710
Huh?

22
00:02:52,370 --> 00:02:53,500
Ah, Shizuka chan?

23
00:02:54,170 --> 00:02:54,380
Huh?

24
00:02:55,630 --> 00:02:57,090
, sorry! I forgot!

25
00:02:57,380 --> 00:02:59,800
be right there!

26
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:04,680
forgot that I promised to do homework with Shizuka!

27
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:06,010
You should get goingthen

28
00:03:06,090 --> 00:03:09,010
But can't miss this episode of Masked Lion

29
00:03:09,390 --> 00:03:10,970
Then you should stay

30
00:03:10,970 --> 00:03:14,430
But if I break my promise, Shizuka chan will
be angry with me. What should I do?

31
00:03:15,520 --> 00:03:16,810
You should make up your mind!

32
00:03:17,850 --> 00:03:18,440
Of course!

33
00:03:20,730 --> 00:03:24,190
Ajust need to become two people..

34
00:03:24,190 --> 00:03:26,440
Good luck with that...

35
00:03:28,280 --> 00:03:28,780
Hub?

36
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:31,780
I did it! It worked!

37
00:03:32,570 --> 00:03:34,740
From the clothes to the sword, a perfect match!

38
00:03:35,530 --> 00:03:39,330
I'll take care of the TV and leave the homework to you.

39
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:42,960
No nothink you should take care of the homework.

40
00:03:43,120 --> 00:03:43,420
Hmm?

41
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:46,340
You little... Just who do you think you are?

42
00:03:47,090 --> 00:03:48,670
Heyhey, hey!

43
00:03:48,670 --> 00:03:50,920
You... what do you think you're doing?

44
00:03:51,090 --> 00:03:53,260
NOBITA!

45
00:03:54,970 --> 00:03:56,390
Draw straws!

46
00:03:57,550 --> 00:03:57,720
Okay

47
00:04:02,470 --> 00:04:04,640
This is unfair!

48
00:04:05,350 --> 00:04:08,980
But, I'll be together with Shizuka chanThat's okay.I guess.

49
00:04:09,100 --> 00:04:09,900
Hey Nobita!

50
00:04:11,270 --> 00:04:13,020
You're playing baseball with us. Let's go

51
00:04:13,610 --> 00:04:16,030
Uh, today can't... ...

52
00:04:16,240 --> 00:04:17,400
What did you say?

53
00:04:18,650 --> 00:04:19,780
Okayokay

54
00:04:20,240 --> 00:04:22,070
I'll just split in half, and be right there.

55
00:04:22,570 --> 00:04:24,660
It's a promise. Don't forget!

56
00:04:26,080 --> 00:04:27,160
Iguess I don't have a choice

57
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:31,830
Wow!

58
00:04:32,790 --> 00:04:35,880
Isplit again! Now I'm just a quarter the size.

59
00:04:36,460 --> 00:04:39,340
Which of us has to go play baseball? Janken pon!

60
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:40,420
Darn!

61
00:04:41,260 --> 00:04:43,920
This bag is so heavy... Oh oh oh!

62
00:04:44,010 --> 00:04:47,930
I'll be there as soon as can! Shizuka is waiting!

63
00:04:48,090 --> 00:04:50,720
better hurry.

64
00:04:55,180 --> 00:04:56,890
Oh, Uncle Nobi?

65
00:04:57,140 --> 00:04:58,900
That voice... Nobita-kun?

66
00:04:59,020 --> 00:05:00,310
What happened to your glasses?

67
00:05:00,690 --> 00:05:01,860
live switched to contacts.

68
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:04,230
But then I dropped them...

69
00:05:04,650 --> 00:05:06,400
Please... Help me find them!

70
00:05:07,030 --> 00:05:08,110
I don't have a choice.

71
00:05:08,110 --> 00:05:10,610
fill leave half of myself here to help.

72
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:15,490
Ogh, soheavy...!

73
00:05:15,580 --> 00:05:17,910
be there as soon as we find them!

74
00:05:18,040 --> 00:05:19,410
I'm relying on you.

75
00:05:20,540 --> 00:05:21,910
It's heading your way, Nobita!

76
00:05:21,910 --> 00:05:23,330
Back! Back!

77
00:05:23,540 --> 00:05:24,790
Ah, man...

78
00:05:25,710 --> 00:05:28,460
Ugh, it's heavy!

79
00:05:32,260 --> 00:05:33,880
NOBITA!

80
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:35,590
You're fired!

81
00:05:40,890 --> 00:05:42,430
Phew, thank goodness!

82
00:06:00,700 --> 00:06:02,070
Help me!

83
00:06:08,830 --> 00:06:10,160
Pervert!

84
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,120
No no no... I didn't mean to do any thing...

85
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:16,960
I'm just having a really bad day...

86
00:06:17,170 --> 00:06:22,380
! Wait! Hey, let me go! Hey!

87
00:06:24,090 --> 00:06:24,720
Here it is!

88
00:06:25,090 --> 00:06:27,050
What a relief!

89
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:28,050
Here you go.

90
00:06:28,050 --> 00:06:30,100
Thanks! Let me get you a soda in return.

91
00:06:30,470 --> 00:06:32,010
SorryI have to go!

92
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:38,190
hope that me who went to do homework is okay.

93
00:06:38,810 --> 00:06:39,690
Huh?

94
00:06:39,850 --> 00:06:40,860
Hey!

95
00:06:41,400 --> 00:06:43,070
Help me!

96
00:06:43,270 --> 00:06:45,030
What are you doing up there?

97
00:06:45,230 --> 00:06:47,820
Just get me down from here quick!

98
00:06:48,150 --> 00:06:52,160
UghI hate climbing trees.

99
00:06:57,620 --> 00:07:00,960
I'm going to fall! Help me!

100
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:02,750
Stop flailing!

101
00:07:04,670 --> 00:07:06,340
Ahhhhh!!!!

102
00:07:09,550 --> 00:07:12,340
We better hurry! Shizuka's not going to be happy!

103
00:07:13,220 --> 00:07:14,880
One-two! One-two!

104
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:19,890
Don't miss next week's episode of Masked Lion"!

105
00:07:20,140 --> 00:07:22,100
Phewthat was amusing!

106
00:07:23,680 --> 00:07:26,730
Hey put me and my half back together.

107
00:07:27,270 --> 00:07:29,190
will once this show is over.

108
00:07:30,940 --> 00:07:33,150
Alright, Shizukachan's been waiting!

109
00:07:34,650 --> 00:07:35,980
Shizukachan!

110
00:07:36,240 --> 00:07:36,490
Hube

111
00:07:37,110 --> 00:07:38,070
Beright there!

112
00:07:39,990 --> 00:07:41,360
Aren't you late?

113
00:07:42,780 --> 00:07:44,370
What were you doing?

114
00:07:45,700 --> 00:07:50,000
thought some help would make the work go faster.

115
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:51,540
Oh.

116
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:54,330
No no, that's not right.

117
00:07:54,330 --> 00:07:54,750
Huh?

118
00:07:54,750 --> 00:07:56,340
No, that's not it at all!

119
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:58,130
Yeah, that's it!

120
00:07:58,130 --> 00:07:58,630
No no no!

121
00:07:58,920 --> 00:08:01,710
told you that's wrongThat's not the answer!

122
00:08:01,710 --> 00:08:04,300
Nodefinitely right!

123
00:08:04,720 --> 00:08:06,970
being so stubborn!

124
00:08:06,970 --> 00:08:07,890
What!?

125
00:08:07,890 --> 00:08:10,760
Shut up! Why should I trust you?

126
00:08:10,760 --> 00:08:12,600
told you, you're wrong!

127
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:14,310
I'm right!

128
00:08:14,310 --> 00:08:16,230
NoI'm right!

129
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:19,770
Why are you fighting with yourself? Stop it!!

130
00:08:23,770 --> 00:08:24,860
Oh, boy...

131
00:08:47,210 --> 00:08:47,750
Hmm?

132
00:08:48,710 --> 00:08:49,750
Nobita-kun

133
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:51,760
Napping, again?

134
00:08:51,960 --> 00:08:56,090
NOBITA!

135
00:08:56,430 --> 00:08:57,470
Nobita-kun?

136
00:08:58,050 --> 00:09:00,760
What's wrong? Get up!

137
00:09:01,680 --> 00:09:05,600
Doraemon? You've been such a good friend...

138
00:09:05,890 --> 00:09:07,940
What happened?

139
00:09:08,100 --> 00:09:10,230
It's over for me...

140
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:13,860
Mama's ring, grandma's heirloom...

141
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:20,150
Shizukachan will be surprised to see this!

142
00:09:20,150 --> 00:09:21,030
NOBITA!

143
00:09:21,610 --> 00:09:22,660
Oh!

144
00:09:26,370 --> 00:09:27,620
Hey! Wait!

145
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:33,750
I've been so worried, haven't been able to concentrate in class.

146
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:35,420
You're never able to concentrate.

147
00:09:36,130 --> 00:09:38,670
definitely get a zero on the test tomorrow.

148
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:39,710
Oh huh.

149
00:09:40,550 --> 00:09:44,630
Mama will scold me, and lose all interest in studying.

150
00:09:45,300 --> 00:09:51,760
My grades will plummet, and never finish elementary school!

151
00:09:52,140 --> 00:09:55,350
That's awfully pessimistic.

152
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:59,850
In that case, why don't you try this out?

153
00:10:00,400 --> 00:10:03,940
Lost Object Recovery Machine

154
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:04,480
Okay

155
00:10:05,530 --> 00:10:08,900
Picture in your mind the ring you lost.

156
00:10:09,240 --> 00:10:10,450
As clearly as you can.

157
00:10:11,410 --> 00:10:15,120
RingRingMama's ring!

158
00:10:15,950 --> 00:10:18,370
Then, you just turn this dial...

159
00:10:22,330 --> 00:10:22,540
Oh!

160
00:10:28,670 --> 00:10:31,130
Wow! That's it!

161
00:10:31,340 --> 00:10:34,630
Alright! I'm saved!

162
00:10:34,800 --> 00:10:37,800
Okay now you can study.

163
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:39,760
Hold on, wait!

164
00:10:39,760 --> 00:10:41,220
Does that machine work on any thing?

165
00:10:41,470 --> 00:10:43,470
Yeah, if you remember the shape...

166
00:10:43,770 --> 00:10:45,850
but you really should be studying.

167
00:10:46,690 --> 00:10:49,350
First, I have some things I want back!

168
00:10:59,030 --> 00:10:59,780
Amazing!

169
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:05,410
That given up on youonly to have you return! It's like a dream!

170
00:11:05,490 --> 00:11:07,200
Alrightfill go for a thousand yen, next.

171
00:11:09,580 --> 00:11:12,210
A thousand yen. A thousand yen.

172
00:11:14,540 --> 00:11:16,040
Hey, it's not coming out.

173
00:11:16,340 --> 00:11:17,710
When did you lose it?

174
00:11:18,340 --> 00:11:20,090
I didn't really lose it...

175
00:11:20,340 --> 00:11:21,630
it okay it just spent it?

176
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:25,590
Stop this, and get studying!!

177
00:11:26,390 --> 00:11:28,090
Don't get so angry.

178
00:11:29,050 --> 00:11:33,060
With this brain, it doesn't really matter if I study or not

179
00:11:33,810 --> 00:11:35,640
What, what did you say?

180
00:11:35,930 --> 00:11:37,230
I'm through with this!

181
00:11:37,810 --> 00:11:40,440
Grrr...

182
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:43,860
I wonder if there's anything else live lost?

183
00:11:44,530 --> 00:11:44,980
Ah, of course!

184
00:11:45,610 --> 00:11:47,650
It's gone! My ring is gone!

185
00:11:48,360 --> 00:11:49,610
Where, where is it?

186
00:11:51,820 --> 00:11:55,160
That's terrible! I can't believe you lost mother's heirloom

187
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:59,040
What, what can I do?

188
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:01,330
Where did it gol?

189
00:12:04,330 --> 00:12:06,340
Mama, are you looking for something?

190
00:12:07,630 --> 00:12:09,170
No no, there's nothing wrong

191
00:12:10,510 --> 00:12:11,840
My wallet!

192
00:12:12,470 --> 00:12:14,680
lost my wallet!

193
00:12:14,680 --> 00:12:18,430
Your wallet? That's no good. Wait here a sec.

194
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:23,720
What should do?

195
00:12:24,680 --> 00:12:29,690
Ha ha! All the manga Mama threw away!

196
00:12:34,190 --> 00:12:36,610
This too?

197
00:12:36,990 --> 00:12:39,860
Oh, right hid this in one of the manga

198
00:12:42,200 --> 00:12:43,200
Oh.

199
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:46,620
Wait! I'm still using that!

200
00:12:47,200 --> 00:12:51,540
Focus on the thing you lost, and it'll come back to you.

201
00:12:51,540 --> 00:12:55,540
Thank you! I'll try it out right now.

202
00:12:59,090 --> 00:12:59,920
Huh?

203
00:13:02,300 --> 00:13:05,720
RingRingRing

204
00:13:07,930 --> 00:13:08,260
Hub?

205
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:12,470
It really worked!

206
00:13:12,470 --> 00:13:15,520
The ringis gone!

207
00:13:22,520 --> 00:13:24,980
Hey, Nobita-kun!

208
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:31,490
Doraemon, please give me back that machine.

209
00:13:31,490 --> 00:13:33,950
promise I'll only use it one more time.

210
00:13:33,950 --> 00:13:38,290
Do you promise you'll study right after?

211
00:13:38,290 --> 00:13:40,000
I do. I do.

212
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:42,160
Okay, I'll give you ten minutes.

213
00:13:43,170 --> 00:13:44,670
Thank you!

214
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:53,880
Grandma, I won't lose this again.

215
00:13:56,090 --> 00:13:57,390
RingRing

216
00:13:58,600 --> 00:13:59,260
There it is!

217
00:14:01,390 --> 00:14:04,140
It's gone. The ring is gone!

218
00:14:04,890 --> 00:14:06,520
How could that happen?

219
00:14:07,770 --> 00:14:09,650
Thank goodness!

220
00:14:10,150 --> 00:14:15,400
Okay, now get back all the toys live ever lost.

221
00:14:15,610 --> 00:14:17,900
Where could I have dropped it?

222
00:14:19,450 --> 00:14:19,820
Oh!

223
00:14:20,110 --> 00:14:22,570
You don't happen to be looking for a ringdo you?

224
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:24,490
How do you know that?

225
00:14:24,870 --> 00:14:26,330
We saw it, didn't we?

226
00:14:26,410 --> 00:14:29,040
Nobita lost an expensivelooking ring around here.

227
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:29,410
Hub?

228
00:14:29,750 --> 00:14:31,830
He didn't tell you?

229
00:14:32,750 --> 00:14:35,540
We probably shouldn't have told you that. Hahaha!

230
00:14:36,920 --> 00:14:38,880
Nobi-chan!

231
00:14:48,350 --> 00:14:48,970
That's...

232
00:14:49,680 --> 00:14:51,310
Ah, Mrs. Nobi.

233
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:55,730
Ah, SenseiHow are you today?

234
00:14:55,730 --> 00:14:57,640
Actuallythis is good timing

235
00:14:57,640 --> 00:14:58,810
Something about my son?

236
00:14:59,150 --> 00:15:03,020
Nobi kun was inattentive all day long today...

237
00:15:10,150 --> 00:15:12,530
haven't used this since kindergarten.

238
00:15:16,330 --> 00:15:18,750
Everyone called me "baby" and laughed at me.

239
00:15:22,460 --> 00:15:26,460
The taste of rubber brings back memories.

240
00:15:29,210 --> 00:15:31,260
Things were good back then.

241
00:15:32,090 --> 00:15:36,090
No one ever hounded me to study.

242
00:15:36,510 --> 00:15:39,890
Nobita, it's been twenty minutes...

243
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:42,680
Everyday, all had to do was play, eat, and sleep.

244
00:15:42,680 --> 00:15:44,980
Hey, how old are you?

245
00:15:45,270 --> 00:15:47,560
you have so much time to think about the past...

246
00:15:47,730 --> 00:15:49,940
You should spend more time thinking about the future!

247
00:15:49,940 --> 00:15:50,860
The future?

248
00:15:51,520 --> 00:15:54,980
There's nothing good in my future...

249
00:15:56,070 --> 00:15:59,700
I'm stupid, and I fail at whatever I do.

250
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:04,580
The only time I was happy was when my grandma was alive...

251
00:16:04,580 --> 00:16:05,660
Nobita!

252
00:16:06,120 --> 00:16:06,740
Mama!

253
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:08,200
just met with your teacher

254
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,370
He told me you were screwing around all class!

255
00:16:12,330 --> 00:16:13,920
I have a reason for that...

256
00:16:14,790 --> 00:16:16,500
don't want to hear any excuses.

257
00:16:16,920 --> 00:16:20,130
It's nothing but excuses from you.

258
00:16:21,130 --> 00:16:22,210
That's...

259
00:16:23,630 --> 00:16:26,260
That's because you always get mad at me.

260
00:16:27,090 --> 00:16:29,300
Is that why you didn't tell me about the ring?

261
00:16:29,510 --> 00:16:29,800
Huh?

262
00:16:30,390 --> 00:16:31,680
I'm disappointed with you.

263
00:16:32,470 --> 00:16:36,640
Anywayyour lack of motivation is the
reason you always get into trouble.

264
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:43,520
What would grandma say if she saw you now?

265
00:16:44,020 --> 00:16:48,280
If grandma were alive, she'd tell you not to nag me so much.

266
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:49,030
What?

267
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:50,490
After all, I'm...

268
00:16:50,990 --> 00:16:53,320
I'm just a worthless human being!

269
00:16:53,780 --> 00:16:55,160
Get out of my way!

270
00:17:09,170 --> 00:17:10,380
Grandma.

271
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:15,180
Ireally want to go back to that time...

272
00:17:19,260 --> 00:17:21,640
Oh, did you really do it againNobi chan?

273
00:17:22,140 --> 00:17:23,850
It's okay

274
00:17:24,230 --> 00:17:25,810
It's just a little mistake

275
00:17:26,310 --> 00:17:29,230
Nobi-chan you've really gotten big!

276
00:17:30,940 --> 00:17:33,980
What an interesting pattern you've made!

277
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:36,280
It's okay.

278
00:17:36,570 --> 00:17:39,860
cast a charm...

279
00:17:40,150 --> 00:17:42,740
to make sure there are no leaks tonight, okay?

280
00:17:46,990 --> 00:17:48,370
She was so nice.

